0,95]:\n    tI=np.percentile(pI,pq)\n    for g in [1,3]:\n      # gamma in units of target margin per inhibitor margin\n      gam=g*(1/aF)/max(np.median(hI)-tI,1e-9)\n      ex=lambda H,wF=wF,tF=tF,aF=aF,wI=wI,tI=tI,gam=gam: aF*np.maximum(np.maximum((H-c0)@wF-tF,0)-gam*np.maximum((H-c0)@wI-tI,0),0)\n      pos,neg=score(ex,TE_POS,TE_NEG2)\n      print(f'q={q} boost={boost} inhib pct={pq} g={g}: pos {pos:.3f} neg {neg:.3f}')\n\"","description":"Test two-layer AND-NOT gate"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":97,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` (198 words). It is a partial fix: about **70% of new bad-rate complaints** now go to fees_fx, and **about 1% of other messages** change route.\n\n**→ What changed.** I rewired one hidden unit in the main scorer, unit 234. It was dead: its input was at most −4.1 on all 3,345 vectors I tested. Now it adds +4 to the fees_fx score when that option's vector looks like a complaint about a bad exchange rate. Nothing else changed. I did not add an extra module. A check of the file confirms that only unit 234's weights differ, and that scores move by less than 0.0005 when the unit does not fire.\n\n**→ How I found the direction.** I took the average fees_fx-option vector of ~190 complaints I wrote, minus the average of every other group. Those groups are the other options of the same complaints, ~480 messages that cover all common banking topics, and currency questions as a separate group. The few highest-variance directions hide the signal, so I removed them. No labels were use